Package: hypertabular
Type: Package
Title: Forward-Only Reads of Delimited Text and Workbooks, Every Cell a Verdict
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Brian", "Buvinghausen", email = "buvinghausen@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Skunk Werkx", role = "cph")
  )
Description: Reads delimited text and 'XLSX', 'ODS' and 'Numbers' workbooks a batch at a
    time into typed columns, under a dialect, a plan of columns and the formats, field
    orders, precisions and epochs the caller declares rather than guesses. Every cell is
    judged by the 'hypercast' package's casts and comes back as its verdict: the value, or a
    closed reason (empty, malformed, out of range) with the offending span of the cell's
    text. A file that is structurally broken comes back as a failure value after every
    intact row before it. The work is done by a compiled 'Rust' core shared with the
    project's bindings for other languages, which neither allocates nor panics; no read
    signals an error for its data.
